PURPOSE Generate the paper's vehicle and package space-time layers at an epoch.
INPUT InputDataset and time-grid, cost, operational and commitment configuration
OUTPUT complete arc catalogs, adjacency, source/sink and transfer metadata
REFERENCES RoadNetwork.GetArc; paper arc tables and Eqs. 1-4, 17
RULE CATALOG ../specs/NETWORK_RULES.md

PROCEDURE TravellingCost(firstPoint,secondPoint,convention)
    IF convention == retained_coordinate_network
        distance := floor(EuclideanDistance(firstPoint,secondPoint))
        return distance,distance,distance
    ELSE
        return declared distance,mode-specific travel duration,generalized cost

PROCEDURE AddTimedArc(owner,family,i,t,j,duration,cost,catalogs)
    tPrime := t + duration
    REQUIRE duration >= 0 and both endpoints lie on the declared time grid
    REQUIRE endpoint states, windows, mode and zone satisfy the family rule
    create immutable recordId and full owner/state/time endpoint identities
    preserve distinct family records even when their endpoint coordinates coincide
    add the record once to owner/family, incoming/outgoing and endpoint indexes
    store duration, cost, service events and SupportKey(record)
    return record

PROCEDURE BuildNetwork(input,config)
    orders := input.orders; vehicles := input.vehicles
    catalogs := empty owner-indexed maps and adjacency
    rules := paper_catalog from RULE CATALOG
    instantiate arrival, departure and passing states at each service location
    instantiate vehicle origins/returns, terminals, transfer states and virtual ends
    FOR each physical vehicle k
        apply ADR zone/reachability or LT terminal/schedule restrictions
        enumerate all rule-permitted point pairs and departure times
        instantiate vehicle families 1..13:
            start, end, travel, loading, unloading, dwelling,
            wait-load I/II, wait-unload I/II, transfer I/II, unused
        for every instance derive endpoints, windows, duration and cost from rules
        AddTimedArc for every feasible instance
    FOR each order r
        enumerate its permitted service/terminal states and departure times
        instantiate package families 1..15:
            start, end, travel, loaded, unloaded, dwelling,
            wait-pickup I/II, wait-dropoff I/II, transfer I/II, unserved,
            carried-through pickup, carried-through dropoff
        permit handover only at declared locations/times and when allowed for r
        add its unserved arc with penalty pi[r] unless service is already committed
        AddTimedArc for every feasible instance
        mark families 3..10,14,15 as the supported carriage subset A_phi[r]
    create one super-source/sink per owner joining all legal start/end times
        so its total layer flow is one, not one unit at each possible start time
    build compatible package/vehicle arc mapping using full state transitions
    IF input carries DynamicState
        preserve committed records and residual sources supplied by that state
        disallow new departures before release of an in-progress vehicle
    return catalogs with ordered indexes, ruleset ID, costs and input fingerprint

PROCEDURE ImportLocalCatalog(originalRecords,config)
    preserve original record identities, endpoint decorations, times and costs
    map roles using RULE CATALOG without manufacturing absent source records
    return catalog with rulesetId=retained_source and an explicit coverage report

PROCEDURE CheckPath(orderedArcs,source,sink,config)
    REQUIRE first tail == source and last head == sink
    REQUIRE consecutive arcs join at identical owner/state/time keys
    REQUIRE every arc belongs to the declared catalog and satisfies its rule
    REQUIRE no repeated record or disconnected selected component
    check service order, time windows and sum of vehicle arc durations <= dutyLimit
    validate transfer pairs and support/load through ValidatePlan for coupled paths
    return valid or a failed condition with its record IDs

ASSUMPTIONS
    Zero-time connectors follow a declared state order. Catalogs without such an
    order require cycle-elimination constraints to obtain connected paths.
    Use the endpoint/index conventions in RULE CATALOG for generation and matching.
    ImportLocalCatalog preserves the records and costs produced by the C# builder.
